 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "For the given K-flat complex P, the exact inverse image F_A P is K-flat. The normalized scalar/tensor isomorphism gives e_QP followed by the tensorator of Q, the total-tensor/single-complex comparison and the localized ordinary balancing map equal to the restricted scalar-extension representative. Use the same equation on F_A P. The ordinary balancing map sends m tensor b to b tensor m; its inverse sends b tensor m to m tensor b. The balancing relations show these are inverse linear maps before sheafification, and hence after sheafification. Since P and F_A P are K-flat, the tensorators of Q in these equations are invertible. Thus the restricted scalar-extension representative maps on these two complexes are invertible.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-pur-derived-change-of-rings",
    "lem-pur-change-of-rings-tensor-comparison",
    "lem-weil-pbc-ringed-topoi-derived-tensor-pullback"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
