    "place": "Tags 07A4, 0G7E and 07A7; coefficient compatibility in more-etale.tex, Tag 0GL6"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "Apply exact restriction U_Z to the assumed representative normalization of c at P. Substitute the scalar/tensor representative equations from step 1. The exact restriction/pullback square is the localization of the ordinary sheaf comparison. The counit square specifying the derived inverse-image tensor comparison identifies it with the ordinary monoidal comparison on the same representatives.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-pur-derived-change-of-rings",
    "lem-sbc-canonical-restrict-scalars-functor-comparisons",
    "def-kun-projection-formula-map",
    "lem-weil-pbc-ringed-topoi-derived-tensor-pullback"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/stacks-project/sites-cohomology.tex",
    "place": "Tags 07A4, 0G7E and 07A7; coefficient compatibility in more-etale.tex, Tag 0GL6"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "The two remaining ordinary sheaf composites agree. Before sheafification, evaluate on a pulled-back pure tensor m tensor b: the scalar balancing map only reverses the coefficient and module factors, the ordinary scalar/pullback conjugate retains both factors, and the coefficient-unit comparison carries the pulled-back unit to the unit. The conjugate and restriction/pullback comparisons have this action because their defining Hom-equivalence equations preserve the composite adjunction units; taking the sheaf pullback adjoint transpose reduces their equality to those unit equations. Both composites therefore give the same tensor. Pure tensors generate, and sheafification preserves this equality. Apply the equality degreewise to P; the coefficient is in degree zero, so no interchange of complex degrees or sign is involved. Cancel the invertible tensor and representative maps of step 1 and the exact geometric representative maps to obtain the displayed equality at Q(P). This uses no flatness of B over A.",
